    "problem_statement": "Table sorting returns incorrect order when using numeric values\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen sorting a TextTable with numeric values, the sort order is incorrect. The table appears to be sorted in reverse order compared to what's expected.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport textfsm.texttable as texttable\n\n# Create a simple table with text data\nt = texttable.TextTable()\nt.header = ('Col1', 'Col2', 'Col3')\nt.Append(('lorem', 'ipsum', 'dolor'))\nt.Append(('ut', 'enim', 'ad'))\nt.Append(('duis', 'aute', 'irure'))\n\n# Sort the table\nt.sort()\n\n# Check the order - should be alphabetical by first column\nprint(\"Row 1:\", t[1].values)  # Expected: ['duis', 'aute', 'irure']\nprint(\"Row 2:\", t[2].values)  # Expected: ['lorem', 'ipsum', 'dolor'] \nprint(\"Row 3:\", t[3].values)  # Expected: ['ut', 'enim', 'ad']\n```\n\nThe sorting appears to work in reverse - rows that should come first are appearing last and vice versa. This affects both default sorting and custom key-based sorting operations."
